    "body": "Turns out a completely fresh datadir means there is no chain state to load and hence no detection of a lagging clock occurs in that subsystem. Instead we do proceed into attempting to start a headers sync.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Diff to repro with fresh -datadir</summary>\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n--- a/src/init.cpp\r\n+++ b/src/init.cpp\r\n@@ -1499,6 +1499,8 @@ bool AppInitMain(NodeContext& node, interfaces::BlockAndHeaderTipInfo* tip_info)\r\n     const ArgsManager& args = *Assert(node.args);\r\n     const CChainParams& chainparams = Params();\r\n \r\n+    SetMockTime(chainparams.GenesisBlock().Time() - 3h);\r\n+\r\n     auto opt_max_upload = ParseByteUnits(args.GetArg(\"-maxuploadtarget\", DEFAULT_MAX_UPLOAD_TARGET), ByteUnit::M);\r\n     if (!opt_max_upload) {\r\n         return InitError(strprintf(_(\"Unable to parse -maxuploadtarget: '%s'\"), args.GetArg(\"-maxuploadtarget\", \"\")));\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nFollow-up to #35351",
    "labels": [
      {
